  <h2>Sizing: The #1 Reason for Returns</h2>
  <p>In the activewear industry, fit is everything. A customer who loves the design but hates the fit will not return. Getting your size charts right from the start is the best way to reduce return rates and build customer loyalty.</p>
  
  <h3>Understanding Global Standards</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>US Sizing:</strong> Generally larger with more room in the hips and bust. Often uses "Vanity Sizing."</li>
    <li><strong>EU Sizing:</strong> More tailored and true-to-measurements. Follows a more athletic, leaner cut.</li>
    <li><strong>Asian Sizing:</strong> Significantly smaller and shorter in length. Often 1-2 sizes smaller than US standards.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Stretch Factor & Tolerance</h3>
  <p>Because activewear is high-stretch, you must consider the "Compression Level." A high-compression legging might need a slightly different size chart than a soft yoga legging to maintain comfort.</p>

  <h3>Creating Your Brand's "Perfect Fit"</h3>
  <p>At Fitclo, we provide standard base patterns for US and EU markets. We highly recommend ordering a full size-run of samples (S, M, L, XL) to perform fit-tests on real models before committing to mass production.</p>
</GuideLayout>
